infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Per-op vs batched: pay the fixed cost F N times or once
  desc Same hardware, same data — only how often you pay F changes the result
  compares
    - label Per-op: N × (F + V)
      children
        - label Redis: 10k PINGs in 1.19s
          desc One RTT + ACK paid per command
        - label Kafka: ~8k msg/s
          desc Produce request + replication ACK per message
        - label Postgres: 10M rows in 9000s
          desc Parse + plan + commit + WAL flush per row
    - label Batched: F + N × V
      children
        - label Redis pipelined: 0.25s (~5×)
          desc One RTT for the whole batch
        - label Kafka batched: ~150k msg/s (~19×)
          desc batch.size + linger.ms amortize the ACK
        - label Postgres COPY: 14s (~640×)
          desc One parse, one commit for all rows
theme
  palette #f43f5e #10b981
